      "id": "source-2",
      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T12:05:00Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the exploit call trace and receipt, creation transaction, direct runtime at creation and immediately before the exploit, the incident post-mortem, and the commit-pinned reproduction. The exploit calls MigrateTroveZap 0xcc7218100da61441905e0c327749972e3cbee9ee directly and abuses its onFlashLoan path to close a victim's trove and reopen it with attacker-selected collateral parameters. The 4,627-byte runtime has hash 0xe055a152b1a5722ee17e61f3b43ee5c9722a9f41ae6a5ec473491e09aa7c3a06 at deployment and immediately before the exploit. Since the contract was deployed after EIP-6780 took effect, the unchanged direct runtime makes deployment the latest possible code-change event."
    },
